{"agda":{"module":"FeatureReachability","names":["Cargo.absent-under-all-features","Monotone.reach-mono"]},"claim":"THY-1","id":"hyperpolymath/mathesis#THY-1","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/theory_praxis.deed","sha256":"e57efc6832f884bc697dd2f99f0073c8d0e765fd0430c438ff604f9d199b9098"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/mathesis","shelf":"theory","source_commit":"10f9f46ff7e1c8a0433164bc8bf6d8f30842fd4c","statement":"In a dependency graph whose edges are guarded by features closed under Horn rules, and by an arbitrary per-target condition, a node unreachable with every feature requested is unreachable under any request, on each target (`Cargo.absent-under-all-features`). The general form is `Monotone.reach-mono`: reachability over a monotone family of edge sets is monotone.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"Applied.Missing","names":["Proofs.closing-needs","Proofs.missing-persists","Proofs.closings-missing","Proofs.verdict-yes","Proofs.breach-decides","Proofs.verdict-missing","Proofs.verdict-not-yes"]},"claim":"APP-1","id":"hyperpolymath/mathesis#APP-1","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/theory_praxis.deed","sha256":"e57efc6832f884bc697dd2f99f0073c8d0e765fd0430c438ff604f9d199b9098"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/mathesis","shelf":"applied","source_commit":"10f9f46ff7e1c8a0433164bc8bf6d8f30842fd4c","statement":"Missing propagates: in the cohort model, an output that depends on a missing input is missing, in every period after it too, and never zero. A verdict is \"no\" on a known breach and otherwise missing when any value it depends on is missing; it is never \"yes\" then.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"Applied.Cash","names":["Proofs.cash-identity"]},"claim":"APP-2","id":"hyperpolymath/mathesis#APP-2","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/theory_praxis.deed","sha256":"e57efc6832f884bc697dd2f99f0073c8d0e765fd0430c438ff604f9d199b9098"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/mathesis","shelf":"applied","source_commit":"10f9f46ff7e1c8a0433164bc8bf6d8f30842fd4c","statement":"Cash identity: the closing cash of the last period equals the opening cash plus, summed over the periods, receipts minus payments; when a value is missing, both sides are missing. Proved for any ordered abelian group; `Applied.IntLaws` proves the integers are one.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"Applied.Cash","names":["Proofs.gap-sound","Proofs.gap-least"]},"claim":"APP-3","id":"hyperpolymath/mathesis#APP-3","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/theory_praxis.deed","sha256":"e57efc6832f884bc697dd2f99f0073c8d0e765fd0430c438ff604f9d199b9098"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/mathesis","shelf":"applied","source_commit":"10f9f46ff7e1c8a0433164bc8bf6d8f30842fd4c","statement":"The funding gap is sound and least: adding the gap to the opening cash keeps every closing balance at or above its floor, and no smaller non-negative amount does. Proved for any ordered abelian group; `Applied.IntLaws` proves the integers are one.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"Applied.Missing","names":["Proofs.members-needs","Proofs.receipts-needs","Proofs.payments-needs","Proofs.closing-needs","Proofs.shortfall-needs","Proofs.cashOk-needs","Proofs.hours-needs","Proofs.capacityOk-needs","Proofs.gap-needs"]},"claim":"APP-4","id":"hyperpolymath/mathesis#APP-4","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/theory_praxis.deed","sha256":"e57efc6832f884bc697dd2f99f0073c8d0e765fd0430c438ff604f9d199b9098"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/mathesis","shelf":"applied","source_commit":"10f9f46ff7e1c8a0433164bc8bf6d8f30842fd4c","statement":"Status never upgrades: the evidence status of an output is never stronger than the weakest status of the inputs that it depends on.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
