{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Instances.Questions","names":["Questions","Questions-dioid","Questions-ordered","Questions-annihilating"]},"claim":"Q-1","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#Q-1","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"`Questions n` (a \"which\" grade over `n` downstream questions) is a `ResourceAlgebra`, `IsDioid`, `IsOrdered` and `IsAnnihilating`. A grade is `n` booleans, `true` where a step loses that question. Its operations are ⊕ = intersection and ⊗ = union, bit by bit, with 𝟘 = every question lost and 𝟙 = none lost.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
