{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Instances.Questions","names":["no-branch-achieves-meet"]},"claim":"Q-4","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#Q-4","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"As alternatives, `collapse ⊕ shuffle` is 𝟙 (no question lost), while neither branch is 𝟙. So ⊕ answers \"is question i kept on some branch?\" and not \"does one branch keep every question?\".","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Morphism","names":["id-hom","_∘h_","id-lax","_∘l_","lax"]},"claim":"F-1","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#F-1","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"Both notions have identities and compose, and every strict morphism is lax.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Morphism","names":["peak-lax"]},"claim":"F-2","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#F-2","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"`peak : HWM → MaxPlus` is lax: the peak of a sequence never exceeds the sum of the peaks.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Morphism","names":["peak-not-strict"]},"claim":"F-3","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#F-3","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"`peak` is not strict: it does not preserve ⊗, whatever it does to the units.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Morphism","names":["no-strict-from-HWM","no-strict-HWM→MaxPlus","no-strict-HWM→Loss"]},"claim":"F-4","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#F-4","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"No strict morphism leaves HWM for an algebra with 𝟘 ≢ 𝟙. In particular, none goes to MaxPlus or to Loss.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Morphism","names":["zero-test-hom","support-hom","Loss→MaxPlus","maps-disagree-at-positive","Loss→MaxPlus-collapses","no-injective-Loss→MaxPlus"]},"claim":"F-5","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#F-5","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"Exactly two strict morphisms Loss → MaxPlus exist, `zero-test` and `support`. Neither distinguishes `fin 1` from `fin 2`.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Morphism","names":["support′-hom","MaxPlus→Loss"]},"claim":"F-6","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#F-6","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"Exactly one strict morphism MaxPlus → Loss exists, `support′`. resource-algebra#3 sketched this direction as \"symmetric\" to Loss → MaxPlus, but it is not: there is one map, not two. The issue's other claim, that every positive grade goes to a single point, holds.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Morphism","names":["loss-bottleneck"]},"claim":"F-7","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#F-7","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"The identity on the carrier is a lax morphism Loss → MinMax: a bottleneck never exceeds the sum.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Morphism","names":["one-question-hom","one-question-needs","one-question-unique"]},"claim":"F-8","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#F-8","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"Out of one question there is exactly one strict morphism into an algebra `B`: lost goes to 𝟘 and kept goes to 𝟙. It exists exactly when `B` has 𝟘 ⊗ 𝟘 ≡ 𝟘, which every annihilating algebra has, and HWM too.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Morphism","names":["first-question","later-questions"]},"claim":"F-9","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#F-9","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"Taking the first question of `Questions (suc n)`, and dropping it, are strict morphisms. Composed, they read any single question alone.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Morphism","names":["count-not-⊕"]},"claim":"F-10","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#F-10","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"The number of lost questions does not preserve ⊕: `collapse` and `shuffle` each count 1 and their ⊕ counts 0. So no map into Loss or MinMax that factors through the count is strict or lax.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Separation","names":["occupancy-is-not-cost"]},"claim":"S-1","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#S-1","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"Sequencing peaks 2 and 3 gives 3 under HWM and 5 under MaxPlus: an occupancy bound is not a cost bound.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Separation","names":["alternatives-differ"]},"claim":"S-2","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#S-2","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"On the same numbers, alternatives give `fin 2` under Loss and `val 3` under MaxPlus: echo's join is min, while tropical's is max.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Separation","names":["maxplus-order","loss-order-reversed"]},"claim":"S-3","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#S-3","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"`val 1 ≼ val 2` in MaxPlus but `fin 2 ≼ fin 1` in Loss: the induced orders run in opposite directions.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Separation","names":["bottleneck-is-not-sum"]},"claim":"S-4","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#S-4","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"Sequencing 2 then 3 gives `fin 5` under Loss but `fin 3` under MinMax: a bottleneck bound is not a loss bound.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Instances.Diamond","names":["Diamond","Diamond-ordered","Diamond-annihilating","Diamond-not-dioid"]},"claim":"C-4b","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#C-4b","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"An annihilating ordered algebra need not be a dioid: the diamond lattice M3 (⊕ = join, ⊗ = meet) is ordered and annihilating but not a dioid, since a ⊗ (b ⊕ c) = a while (a ⊗ b) ⊕ (a ⊗ c) = 𝟘.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Instances.Evidence","names":["Evidence","Evidence-dioid","Evidence-ordered","Evidence-annihilating","≼→≤","≤→≼","≼-proven","⊓e-lowerˡ","⊓e-lowerʳ","⊓e-greatest"]},"claim":"E-1","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#E-1","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"`Evidence`, the PROOF-POLICY §5 statuses as a chain (open-row < tested-only < argued < proven-with-postulates < proven), is a `ResourceAlgebra`, `IsDioid`, `IsOrdered` and `IsAnnihilating`, with ⊕ the stronger and ⊗ the weaker status; ⊗ is the meet of `≼`.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Ledger","names":["eff-≼-own","eff-≼-dep","eff-≼-reach"]},"claim":"E-2","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#E-2","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"Soundness: a ledger row's derived status is no stronger than its own evidence, than any row it depends on, or than any row it reaches through dependencies.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":{"module":"ResourceAlgebra.Ledger","names":["Respects","eff-respects","restrict","eff-greatest"]},"claim":"E-3","id":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra#E-3","kind":"theorem","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/resource-algebra-proofs_praxis.deed","sha256":"735d0044f9783c1d7fcc5443ee347e6987dd92007d4b19f36eb1705c9d4e88a7"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/resource-algebra","source_commit":"c31bf1a9ae9d186674c7ed79c6c9b018a1d59c2b","statement":"Maximality: the derived status respects the ledger, and every respectful assignment is below it row by row, so it is the strongest status the ledger supports.","status_doc":"docs/status/PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
{"agda":null,"claim":"ABI-LC-D1","id":"hyperpolymath/proven#ABI-LC-D1","kind":"demonstration","receipt":{"path":"verification/receipts/lifecycle-20261125/engineering.json","sha256":"653e399024a61d3d990cc31f1e25f052ffbe9ce26b5c84d51f9c80b642992643"},"repo":"hyperpolymath/proven","source_commit":"4ac09e36c6b710099b4ceadb26066a83d949dd8f","statement":"The production Idris lifecycle policy reaches the Linux x86_64 static and shared libraries through the Zig/RefC bridge; actual C and Rust callers observe the specified initialization, shutdown and readiness behavior, and a corrupted generated lifecycle reply is rejected with readiness false.","status_doc":"docs/status/LIFECYCLE-PROOF-STATUS.adoc"}
